2026","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-hip-haus-toronto/events/316022013/","description":"### The Hip Haus presents: [Professionals Networking Event](https://thehiphaus.com \"https://thehiphaus.com\")! Hosted at Aitch\n\n###\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* What is The Hip Haus? \\*\\*\\*\\*The Hip Haus is an organization that exists to empower young and experienced professionals alike in the GTA and help the growth of local business. As professionals (especially post pandemic world) it is sometimes difficult to network with other like minded individuals, get good career advice or simply make connections with others you may be able to help or get help from. The Hip Haus is committed to providing social gatherings in an atmosphere where such networking can take place.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* Who Should Attend? \\*\\*\\*\\*The Hip Haus events are ***19+***. The focus however is the growth and development of professionals in the GTA. It doesn’t matter if you are a business owner, have a job, are looking for a job, recently graduated university/college, still in university/college, looking for others to launch a new idea or just want to meet other professionals, our events are for you.\nRemember that Industry is Industry. One is not better than the other to The Hip Haus. We are expecting a diverse range of industry professionals. Our events in clude professionals from Tech & AI to Entrepreneurs, Musicians, Artists, Bankers, I.T Professionals, Accountants, Investors, Advertising/Marketing Professionals, Bloggers, Authors, Lawyers, Doctors, Dentists (This List Can Clearly Go On). ALL ARE WELCOME!\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* What to Expect at Our Events? \\*\\*\\*\\*Bring Business cards or have your LinkedIn QR code at the ready. Networking! That is the key to these events. Sure it can be a great place to hang out and have a beer with a few friends but it is important to come with an open mind to meet new people and make new connections. Build your network of friends/colleagues/advisors to help yourself as well as them. The Hip Haus wants the professionals of the GTA to come together to help foster personal and professional development.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* Dress Code! \\*\\*\\*\\*This is a tricky one. There is NO strict dress code but remember this; you are meeting professionals in an informal manner and we all know first impressions last forever. Come dressed in a way that would allow you to be comfortable and professional according to your industry. Consider This…would a professional musician/artist necessarily dress the same as an investment banker at work? Be who you are or who you want to be.\n\n#YoungProfessionalsNetworking #ProfessionalsNetworking #EntrepreneurNetworking #FounderEvents #FounderNetworking #AINetworkingToronto #TechNetworkingEvents #YoungProfessionalsAI #EntrepreneursAI #AIandTechToronto #NetworkingEventsGTA #IssabellsToronto\n\n**\\*\\* Let's Get Social!\\*\\*** WEB: [www.thehiphaus.com](http://www.thehiphaus.com/ \"http://www.thehiphaus.com/\") [INSTAGRAM](m/thehiphaus/ \"m/thehiphaus/\") \\| [FACEBOOK](https://www.facebook.com/thehiphaus \"https://www.facebook.com/thehiphaus\") \\| [TWITTER](https://twitter.com/thehiphaus \"https://twitter.com/thehiphaus\")","startDate":"2026-10-15T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Aitch Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"461 King Street West Toronto, ON M5V 3M4, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Hip Haus - Young Professionals Networking","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-hip-haus-toronto/"},"performer":"The Hip Haus - Young Professionals Networking"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"👻 Ghost Walking Tour of Queen West & Yonge Street 🌙","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316200713/","description":"# 👻 Ghost Tour: Queen West & Yonge Street 🌙\n\n### Restless Spirits, Strange Stories & Toronto After Dark\n\nThe thing about ghosts is… **they don’t always stay where they died.**\nSometimes they linger in places they loved. Sometimes they remain where unfinished business keeps them tethered. And sometimes, apparently, they just really like a particular chair.\n\nOn this walking tour, we'll explore some of the stranger stories connected to **Queen West and Yonge Street** — from hospitals and theatres to music halls, historic buildings, and some rather unexpected places.\nSome of these people met their fate on these streets.\n**Most didn't.**\n\nGhosts are funny that way.\n\nThis is a **curated storytelling experience**, combining Toronto history, local legends, and some of the city's more unusual ghost stories.\nAnd don't worry — we're not going inside the buildings.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Explore\n\nWe'll begin outside the **Four Seasons Centre for the Performing Arts** and make our way east toward Yonge Street.\nAlong the way, we'll hear stories about:\n\n* 🔫 **Don't play with guns… again**\n* 🙏 **“This is my hospital,” said the Nun**\n* 🎶 **The spirit who stayed for the music**\n* 🪑 **Who sat in that chair?**\n* 👻 Other strange stories, unexplained encounters, and Toronto legends\n\nWe'll finish at **Yonge-Dundas Square**.\nThe walk will take approximately **90 minutes**, depending on the pace of the group.\n\nWe'll remain outdoors throughout the experience and will **not be entering any buildings**.\n\n***\n\n## 🌙 A Little About the Experience\n\nThis isn't simply a walk where someone points out a few supposedly haunted buildings.\nI've researched the stories, developed the route, and brought the different pieces together into a single experience.\nSome stories are rooted in Toronto history.\nSome have been passed down as local legends.\nAnd some leave you wondering whether there might actually be something to them.\n**You can decide what you believe.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside the **Four Seasons Centre for the Performing Arts**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** **Yonge-Dundas Square**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated ghost-walking experience**, rather than one of our regular social walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and brought together specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support the time and work that goes into creating these walks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n📱 Your phone for photos — if you're brave enough. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 👻 People who love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone interested in Toronto's strange history\n* 🎭 Theatre and music lovers\n* 🕯️ People who enjoy local legends and unexplained stories\n* 🚶 People looking for something different to do in the evening\n* 😂 Anyone who likes being a little scared without taking it too seriously\n\nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the ghosts.**\n**Stay for the stories.**\n**Leave wondering what you just heard.** 👻🌙","startDate":"2026-10-15T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Four Seasons Centre for the Performing Arts","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"145 Queen Street West, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/"},"performer":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Practical Philosophy Meetup - Toronto 🇨🇦 ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/practical-philosophy-club-ontario/events/315596873/","description":"**NO PHILOSOPHY EXPERTISE REQUIRED!**\n\n**🏛️ WHAT'S PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY ABOUT?**\n\nPractical Philosophy is a weekly meet-up that brings critical thinkers together for an opportunity to dive deep on a topic, practice communicating, and building a community. All with no ‘official’ philosophy knowledge required! 😎\n\nPractical Philosophy is based on the idea that philosophy should be accessible to all, and not something reserved only for academics. Each week we choose a topic, and the goal is to use the conversation to develop our critical thinking and communication as we explore that topic.\nThe goal is to help develop our Critical Thinking, Communication, and Community 🙌\n\n**📓 HOW DOES IT WORK?**\n\nEach week, we pick one topic and discuss it. The topic for the week is shared, generally in the [Whatsapp group](https://chat.whatsapp.com/B7LyJIeBlaH5VtXkMJTTph?mode=gi_t), along with jump-off points to get the conversation going.\n\nWhen groups get bigger than 7-8 people, it’s important that we break into smaller groups. This way we are able to maintain a conversational flow as opposed to having our meetups feel like a discourse or lecture.\n\n**General Meeting Agenda**\n\nEach Practical Philosophy meet-up follows this general timeline:\n\n* 19:30-19:45 - People arrive and chat, get to know each other before the official start.\n* 19:45-19:55 - Meeting introduction, explanation of Practical Philosophy and the topic for the week, read the guidelines and the overview so attendees know what to expect in terms of timelines.\n* 19:55-21:15 - Break into small groups - introduce yourselves and general thoughts on the topic, open discussion afterwards. At this point the group can review the ‘jump-off’ questions as needed, but they are just there to help guide the conversation. It’s not obligatory to answer them.\n* 21:15-21:30 - Bring everyone back together to discuss conclusions of the topic - each group gives a short 1-minute summary. Organizer concludes the meeting and everyone takes a group photo.\n* 21:30 - The official meeting is over but it’s a great opportunity to get to know people in a non-structured environment, so we often stick around, chat, and get to know each other.\n\n**🧧PRICING?**\n\nPractical Philosophy is operated entirely on voluntary donations! If we are meeting in a café, buy a beverage! Donations are 100% voluntary, but they help us to bring the gift of deep conversation to people around the world. If you'd like to support, you can [donate here](https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/donation-form/donate-to-practical-philosophy)!\n(Practical Philosophy is a registered Canadian charity)\n\n**💛 WHAT PEOPLE SAY ABOUT PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY**\n\n**🗣** “I feel like Philosophy Club helps someone build their own belief system through a series of perspectives while not promoting what’s right and wrong” - Ekam\n\n🗣 “I got hooked from day 1 and felt it was the right place for me. I feel it is a place where people can go to learn and discuss new perspectives and increase critical thinking and community by interacting with people who might challenge your point of views but at the same time encourage you to have openness and mind flexibility.” - Daniel\n\n**🤓 FAQ**\n\n* **​What will we talk about? What's the topic?**\n\n​The topic for the week is shared every Sunday in the Whatsapp group. We try to add the topic to the comment section on this event page as well but if you don’t see it, the topic and the jump-off points will be in our [Whatsapp](https://chat.whatsapp.com/B7LyJIeBlaH5VtXkMJTTph?mode=gi_t).\n\n* **Do I need to study or read anything to attend?**\n\nNo preparation is necessary. This isn’t a study of other thinkers. We want to know what you think about the topic, not what an old philosopher thought. If you have a perspective from a religion or a school of thought to share, throw it on the table and we’ll discuss it.\n\n* **Is there a specific philosophy that Practical Philosophy is focused on?**\n\nThe goal of our meet-ups is to not have dogmatic discussions, and flex our critical thinking muscles. Because of this, we want to hear from every realm of thought, and don't study a particular school.\n\n* **Is it mostly men that attend?**\n\nSurprisingly, no! Although often, philosophy is seen as a Candelabra affair in a dark room with a bunch of guys, our Practical Philosophy meetups are generally 50/50 between genders, and we don’t meet in any dark rooms.\n\n* **Can I come alone?**\n\nOf course you can, we encourage it :)\n\n* **Can I be late?**\n\nPlease don't be! We do have a 15 minute grace period where we allow people to funnel in while we hang out, but after that if you arrive too late, it disrupts the flow of the conversation.\n\n* **Where do you meet?**\n\nThe location is posted in Meetup and our [Whatsapp](https://chat.whatsapp.com/B7LyJIeBlaH5VtXkMJTTph?mode=gi_t) group for this location. It is HIGHLY RECOMMENDED that you join the Whatsapp group! If you want to know what other cities have a Practical Philosophy Club, you can see our chapters on our [website](https://www.practicalphilosophy.club/practical-philosophy-locations/).\n\n🤝**POLICY**\n\nTo respect our members privacy, we ask that no one privately message a member without first getting explicit consent. (This looks like speaking in person and being asked to message privately.) Contacting or texting other participants without prior consent is not permitted and may result in removal from the group. Practical Philosophy reserves the right to enforce this policy at its discretion to maintain a safe and respectful environment.\n\n**PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY CLUB - Philosophy, everywhere. ✨**\n\nWe started in Practical Philosophy back in 2021 and there are now 50+ chapters in over 25 countries, including Canada, Spain, Japan, Mexico and many more! 🗺️\n\n**\\*\\*\\***\n**Join our Toronto [Whatsapp Group](https://chat.whatsapp.com/B7LyJIeBlaH5VtXkMJTTph?mode=gi_t) 👈**\n**Follow us on [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/practicalphilosophyclub/) 👈**\n**Our [website](https://www.practicalphilosophy.club/) 👈**","startDate":"2026-10-15T23:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Madison Avenue Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"14 Madison Avenue (Bloor & Spadina), Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Practical Philosophy Club - Ontario 🇨🇦","url":"https://www.meetup.com/practical-philosophy-club-ontario/"},"performer":"Practical Philosophy Club - Ontario 🇨🇦"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"👻 Ghost Tour of Queen West & Yonge Street 🌙","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316200720/","description":"# 👻 Ghost Tour: Queen West & Yonge Street 🌙\n\n### Restless Spirits, Strange Stories & Toronto After Dark\n\nThe thing about ghosts is… **they don’t always stay where they died.**\nSometimes they linger in places they loved. Sometimes they remain where unfinished business keeps them tethered. And sometimes, apparently, they just really like a particular chair.\n\nOn this walking tour, we'll explore some of the stranger stories connected to **Queen West and Yonge Street** — from hospitals and theatres to music halls, historic buildings, and some rather unexpected places.\nSome of these people met their fate on these streets.\n**Most didn't.**\n\nGhosts are funny that way.\n\nThis is a **curated storytelling experience**, combining Toronto history, local legends, and some of the city's more unusual ghost stories.\nAnd don't worry — we're not going inside the buildings.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Explore\n\nWe'll begin outside the **Four Seasons Centre for the Performing Arts** and make our way east toward Yonge Street.\nAlong the way, we'll hear stories about:\n\n* 🔫 **Don't play with guns… again**\n* 🙏 **“This is my hospital,” said the Nun**\n* 🎶 **The spirit who stayed for the music**\n* 🪑 **Who sat in that chair?**\n* 👻 Other strange stories, unexplained encounters, and Toronto legends\n\nWe'll finish at **Yonge-Dundas Square**.\nThe walk will take approximately **90 minutes**, depending on the pace of the group.\n\nWe'll remain outdoors throughout the experience and will **not be entering any buildings**.\n\n***\n\n## 🌙 A Little About the Experience\n\nThis isn't simply a walk where someone points out a few supposedly haunted buildings.\nI've researched the stories, developed the route, and brought the different pieces together into a single experience.\nSome stories are rooted in Toronto history.\nSome have been passed down as local legends.\nAnd some leave you wondering whether there might actually be something to them.\n**You can decide what you believe.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside the **Four Seasons Centre for the Performing Arts**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** **Yonge-Dundas Square**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated ghost-walking experience**, rather than one of our regular social walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and brought together specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support the time and work that goes into creating these walks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n📱 Your phone for photos — if you're brave enough. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 👻 People who love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone interested in Toronto's strange history\n* 🎭 Theatre and music lovers\n* 🕯️ People who enjoy local legends and unexplained stories\n* 🚶 People looking for something different to do in the evening\n* 😂 Anyone who likes being a little scared without taking it too seriously\n\nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the ghosts.**\n**Stay for the stories.**\n**Leave wondering what you just heard.** 👻🌙","startDate":"2026-10-15T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Four Seasons Centre for the Performing Arts","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"145 Queen St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Convos, Bites & Banter 🤣 (Gladstone Hotel)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-cuw-club-singlewomenwithoutchildren/events/316571915/","description":"Hey ladies!\n\nLet's check out Cassette at **The Gladstone Hotel** on Queen West for some convo games, rants 😂 and storytelling. 🍸💬✨\n\n**EVENT:**\n**Open Ended** is a social \"storytellers and storylisteners\" night inspired by conversation cards, hot takes, and random topics to get everyone chatting!\n\nThis would be such a vibe as a group! 🙌🏾 Some topics can be kept at the table, and some can be shared with the room (you can always change the names to protect the \"innocent\" 🤣)\n\nThere is a \"live storytelling element\", but **NO pressure for everyone to \"grab the mic\"** (but we will support you if you do 👩🏿‍🦱 👩🏼 👩🏽‍🦱 !)\n\n**Once confirmed**, tickets will be purchased together so no one is truly \"solo\".\n\n**VENUE:** 📍\nCassette is a newish restaurant/bar near Queen & Gladstone, carrying an artsy/social energy with a range of live music, comedy, karaoke, trivia and community events.\n\nCheck out their [menu](https://www.cassetteto.com/menu) below for cocktails, comfort food and more! Any food and drink ordered will be at **your own expense**:\nhttps://www.cassetteto.com/menu\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**IMPORTANT:**\n*A **minimum number** is required to proceed as a \"group\". Once CONFIRMED, I'll collect payment in advance in a week or so. **This meetup is ONLY for the group purchase.***\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n**DETAILS:** 🎟️\n\n* Sign up to the waitlist to join us!\n* At the time of posting, tickets are $25 ($20 + SCSC's $5 non-refundable RSVP fee)\n* Etransfers will be required in advance\n* All ticket sales are final (as per ticket seller)\n\nHere's a sample of [their last \"Open Ended\"](https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/open-ended-a-storytelling-night-tickets-1994954486572) event:\nhttps://www.eventbrite.ca/e/open-ended-a-storytelling-night-tickets-1994954486572\n\nLooking forward to seeing both new and familiar faces!","startDate":"2026-10-15T23:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Gladstone House","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1214 Queen St W, Toronto, ON M6J 1J6, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Solo & Childfree* Social Club (for Women ONLY - 30s/40s/50s)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-cuw-club-singlewomenwithoutchildren/"},"performer":"Solo & Childfree* Social Club (for Women ONLY - 30s/40s/50s)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"French at the Royal Conservatory","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/316107659/","description":"Join us for an evening of French conversation at B Espresso Bar in the atrium of the Toronto Royal Conservatory of Music (near St. George station)! We welcome all levels of French, and it's free\\*. Venez pratiquer votre français!\n\n\\*While there is no fee to attend this event, guests are expected to purchase something from B Espresso Bar, in accordance with RCM's restrictions on usage of the cafe atrium space.\n\n**Building location:**\nThe Royal Conservatory is at 273 Bloor St W, between Varsity Stadium and the Royal Ontario Museum (ROM). There are entrances off Bloor St. and Philosopher's Walk. If you enter from Bloor St through the large glass doors, follow the hallway on the left beside the staircase and turn left at the end. (Closest TTC: St. George)\n\n**Notes and restrictions:**\nThe host may or may not attend this event. Attendees are encouraged to seat themselves at two or more adjacent tables, as needed. Please form groups of 6 people at each table; do not rearrange chairs and tables to accommodate more people, as this obstructs the narrow walking space. Guests are expected to order something from the cafe, and are asked to please refrain from bringing outside food or drink. Attendees must leave the building at 8pm when the cafe stops serving.\n\n**Contributions:**\nIf you are a regular with us and would like to support the group, please send any contributions by e-transfer to [diskutomeetup@gmail.com.](http://diskutomeetup@gmail.com.) The yearly donation goal and amounts received year-to-date will be tracked anonymously on [this google sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/18GfqYsis8Cf2XGg4KsKQJsY_0Fv3bsSQHwJAxvC1Km8/edit?usp=sharing). Thank you so much for your support.","startDate":"2026-10-15T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Royal Conservatory of Music","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🐾 Give Back: TNR Cat Rescue Volunteer Day","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/events/316773200/","description":"Please read the details before RSVPing.\n\n🐾 Time to give back, guys\n\nWe’ve partnered with a non-profit animal rescue group to support a TNR (Trap-Neuter-Return) campaign in Scarborough, near 75 Birchmount Ave.\n\nWe’re looking for volunteers to help with\n\n1. 🪤 Setting up traps at designated locations\n2. 🚗 Transporting cats to/from the clinic\n3. 🐱 Feeding cats at designated locations\n\nSome activities require access to your own vehicle, while others simply require your time and willingness to help.\n\nEvery little bit helps, and the cats definitely need us. ❤️?\n\nAnyone allergic to cats, furs or anything related to animals, please do not signup\n\nYou participate this in this event at your own risk. Organizers of this meetup or anyone who is part of this campaign isn't responsible for any untoward incident during your participation in this event .","startDate":"2026-10-15T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Scarborough Gardens Arena","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"75 Birchmount Road, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe & Wander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/"},"performer":"Vibe & Wander"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The REAL ESTATE NETWORKING Event ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontorealestateinvestorsclub/events/316650480/","description":"Calling all Real Estate Investors and Industry Professionals!\n\nJoin us for an exciting evening of networking with like-minded professionals that are passionate about Real Estate Investing.\n\nLandlords / Investors / Finance / Realtors / Lawyers / Tax specialists / Engineers / & more!\n\nAdmission & Drinks are FREE - The more the merrier, so bring your friends!\n\nLocated DT Toronto at the SingleKey Headquarters (Queen & Spadina) :\n\n276 Queen St W\nToronto ON M5V 2A1\nCanada","startDate":"2026-10-15T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"SingleKey Headquarters","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"276 Queen St W Toronto ON M5V 2A1 Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Toronto Real Estate Investors Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontorealestateinvestorsclub/"},"performer":"The Toronto Real Estate Investors Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"[CAS] ENG x MANDARIN Board Game Exchange (英语x普通桌游活动)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/canasian-station/events/316703013/","description":"*To join this event, you must be able to speak full sentences in Mandarin.\n\nThis event is for those wanting to practice Mandarin and/or English. Here, you can chat with others and play board games in either language to improve your linguistic skills. Feel free to join our WeChat group during the event, as it is the best way to stay connected with us.\n\nIf you have any questions, leave a comment on this event page.\n\n＜中文版＞\n此活动是以聊天和玩桌游练习中文或英文，等级不限，平时有6-10位参加者。此活动微信群可在活动中加入，互相学习，天天向上。\n\n如果您有任何疑问，请随时在活动页上留言或联系主持人","startDate":"2026-10-15T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"101 College St","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"101 College St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CAS Meetup Community","url":"https://www.meetup.com/canasian-station/"},"performer":"CAS Meetup Community"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Meetup Event: Business Builders — Coffee + Clarity Session","url":"https://www.meetup.com/leadershift/events/316592748/","description":"I get a lot of messages from people who want to connect for different reasons—partnerships, potential investment, help building a leveraged business model, or job opportunities. This meet-up is a casual but **structured** way to meet in person, quickly understand what you’re working on, and determine clear next steps.\n\n### **📍 Location**\n\n**Second Cup**\n4841 Yonge St · North York, ON\n\n### **🕓 Time**\n\n**Aug 20th, 2026**\n**6:00 PM – 9:00 PM**\n\n***\n\n## **💵 Attendance Fee (Important)**\n\n**$10 for business-related attendance**, including:\n\n* business model feedback / guidance\n* partnership discussions\n* investment-related conversations\n* strategic support / “how do I move forward?” planning\n\n*If you’re coming for both job + business advice, it’s considered business-related and the $10 applies.*\n\n***\n\n## **✅ RSVP (Required)**\n\nPlease RSVP so I can plan seating and manage time fairly for everyone.\n\n***\n\n## **What this meet-up is (and isn’t)**\n\n**This is an intro + screening session** designed to:\n\n* meet you briefly\n* clarify your direction\n* identify fit\n* suggest the next best step\n\n**This is not** a full consulting session, a guaranteed job interview, or a promise of investment/partnership. Those decisions happen after follow-up, if there’s a fit.\n\n***\n\n## **Format / Timeboxing**\n\nTo keep it fair, conversations will be **timeboxed (approximately 15–20 minutes per person)** depending on turnout. You may stay and listen to other discussions.\n\n***\n\n## **What to bring (typed + prepared)**\n\n### **If you want help with a business model**\n\nBring a **typed 1-page plan** (rough is fine) including:\n\n* what the business does\n* who the customer is\n* how it makes money\n* what you’ve done so far\n* what you need help with right now\n\n### **If you’re looking for a job**\n\nBring **two printed copies** of your resume.\n\n### **If you want to partner with me**\n\nBring a **typed outline** including:\n\n* your concept (clear + simple)\n* **your responsibilities** (what you will personally do each week)\n* **your expectation of my responsibilities**\n* what success looks like (timeline + goals)\n\n### **If you’re seeking investment (or want to discuss it)**\n\nBring a **typed summary** including:\n\n* what traction you have (sales/users/LOIs/partnerships—anything real)\n* how much capital you’re seeking\n* exactly how the funds would be used\n* why you’re the person/team to execute\n\n***\n\nIf this sounds like you, join me at **Second Cup on Oct 15th from 6:00 PM - 9:00 PM**.\n\nIf you are looking for a job, please use the meetup messaging feature to message me and I will add you to the event.","startDate":"2026-10-15T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Second Cup","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"North York","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"4841 Yonge St, North York, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LeaderSHIFT","url":"https://www.meetup.com/leadershift/"},"performer":"LeaderSHIFT"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Visionary Public Speaking Club - Practice Your Public Speaking Skills With Us ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/visionary-publicspeaking-club/events/316663684/","description":"Are you looking to enhance your public speaking skills and boost your confidence? If so, then join us for an exciting Public Speaking meeting! Get inspired by one of the prepared speeches, or be brave and participate in our fun table topics.\n\nThe meetings at our club provide a save space for you to practice speaking in front of others, receive constructive feedback, and develop your public speaking skills.\n\nWe believe that everyone can learn how to become a great speaker and we welcome everyone who want to join us in person for one of our meetings and improve their public speaking skills.\n\nDon't miss out on this chance to take your public speaking skills to the next level and meet other like-minded individuals. Join us at our next meeting and start building your confidence and leadership skills today!\n\nPlease reach out to the Event Host if you have any questions.\n\nThis event is not hosted by or sponsored by the Toronto Public Library","startDate":"2026-10-15T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Public Library - Fort York Branch","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"190 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Visionary Public Speaking Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/visionary-publicspeaking-club/"},"performer":"Visionary Public Speaking Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Singles Speed Dating Game Night","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/events/316007295/","description":"For tickets and Information:[ https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1991157370295](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1991157370295)\n**IMPORTANT NOTE: CLICKING THE RSVP AND PAY ORGANIZER BUTTON ON MEETUP DOES NOT GET YOU A TICKET/ SPOT. YOU HAVE TO CLICK THE LINK TO THE EVENTBRITE PAGE AND PURCHASE A TICKET THERE. PRICE GOES UP AS EVENT TIME APPROACHES AND MAY SELL OUT SO GET YOUR TICKET ON EVENTBRITE ASAP.**\n\nToronto Dating Games Singles Game Night: Play Fun Icebreaker Games And Match With People (Check dates below for your age range)\nA Dating Games Singles Game Night is a revolutionary new event that is changing the way singles meet. It's a fun new twist on speed dating! Let's face it, we're all tired of the endless online swiping on dating apps and this event is the perfect way to meet other singles in real life.\n***Age Range: 20s, 30s, 40s***\n\n**HOW THE EVENT WORKS...**\n\\- At each Dating Games Singles Event event we book a reserved area with some tables at a cool bar with a great vibe\n\\- After you get your ticket we give you the event reservation name\\.\\.\\. When you arrive you just tell the venue host the reservation name and you'll be directed to the event area where you'll get to meet the other fun singles who are also looking to meet new people\\.\n\n\\- You'll be playing fun and easy icebreaker games to get to know everyone\\.\n\n\\- After the event you'll be a able to login to our app where you'll be able to select the people you'd like to stay in touch with \\(scroll down for more details about how that works\\)\\.\n\n\\- We usually have between 12 and 20 people at each event\\. The amount of people varies from event to event but you'll definitely get to meet a good amount of people without being overwhelmed by a huge crowd\\. We keep the events fairly small and intimate so you really get to know everyone and make real connections\\.\n\\- Our host will walk you through the event via video on your phone \\(so there's no awkward check in process or silly name tags\\)\n\\- The coolest part about the event is that no one else at the venue will even know you're at a singles event\\. It will just look like a group of friends having fun around a table\\!\n\\- During the fun icebreaker games you can order cocktails \\(or non\\-alcoholic mocktails\\) to get everyone talking and then move into the games \\(feel free to order food/appetizers if you'd like to as well\\. Everyone pays for their own tab at the venue\\)\n\n*\\*\\* QUICK NOTE: WE WILL BE RAISING THE TICKET PRICE EVERY FEW DAYS AND BECAUSE WE LIMIT THE SPOTS AVAILABLE, THE EVENT WILL VERY LIKELY SELL OUT BEFORE THE EVENT TIME GRAB YOUR TICKET ASAP TO MAKE SURE YOU GET A SPOT. \\*\\**\n\n**WHAT ARE THE ICEBREAKER GAMES ALL ABOUT?**\nYou'll be playing fun games like \"Friendly Feud\" which is similar to the popular prime time TV show we all know. In this game you and the other singles at the table will be asked fun questions like, \"Name a gift that women love men to give them\". You will try to come up with the most popular answer and then you'll find out if you got the top answer. Another popular game we sometimes play is Blank Slate where you have to try to guess the most popular fill in the blank answer to questions like, _________ TIME . You'd have to try to come up with the most popular answer... is it PARTY TIME? Is it NIGHT TIME? Or maybe it's SHOWTIME.\n**HERE'S THE REALLY COOL PART!**\nThis event has led to countless relationships and new friendships formed because after the event you'll be able to stay in touch with the people you met at the event by reaching out and contacting them on our app. After the event is over we allow you to login to the app and **swipe on the people you'd like to stay in touch with!** It's similar to a dating app but you'll have actually met and mingled with the people in person before deciding if you want to match and stay in touch with them! After you get your ticket you'll be able to upload a photo of yourself on our webpage (only viewable by the other event attendees). After you sign up you will get an email from us with instructions on how to upload your photo to our app/webpage. It's the perfect way to meet someone, merging new technology and good old fashioned meeting in real life!\n\\*\\*\\* IMPORTANT! IF YOU DON'T SEE AN EMAIL FROM US AFTER YOU SIGN UP MAKE SURE TO CHECK YOUR SPAM FOLDER. THAT EMAIL CONTAINS IMPORTANT INFORMATION AND DETAILS ABOUT THE EVENT AND GETTING ONTO THE APP \\*\\*\\*\n*A message we received about one of our recent events: \"I had a great time at the event. The people were really friendly and the games were a lot of fun. It was a refreshing change of pace from the dating apps\" - Leah*\n\\*\\* QUICK NOTE: Because the venue is giving us their valuable table space we ask that you order either a 1 drink minimum or if you don't drink alcohol at least a food item off the menu (can be an appetizer).\n\nFor tickets and Information:[ https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1991157370295](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1991157370295)","startDate":"2026-10-15T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Gatherings Restobar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"49 St Clair Ave West,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/"},"performer":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/d/5/4/highres_535552564.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/a/7/a/highres_535754970.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/8/c/7/highres_535106823.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/d/3/1/highres_506560241.jpeg" as="image" data-next-